  "body": "## What changed\n\n- The Mazak, Fanuc and Doosan DNM posts now lift Z before the preamble of each section after the first.\n- The lift uses the `safeRetract` method of the post: `G91 G28 Z0` (default) or `G53 G00 Z<safeRetractZ>`.\n- The lift comes immediately before the `G90 ... G49 G80` block. The `G90` of that block ends the `G91` of the `G28` lift. `T M6` and `G43 H` follow as before.\n- The first section gets no lift. Single-tool programs do not change.\n- A Go home or a setup-change lift already raises Z. The post then writes no second lift (`zUp` flag).\n- Fanuc and Doosan: a tilted section leaves `G43.4` armed until the next `G49`. The post then writes `G49` before the lift, in the same order as its Go home. The upright return after a tilt (#3466) no longer writes its own lift.\n\n## Cause\n\nEach later preamble wrote `G49` and `T M6` at the clearance height of the previous operation. The Mazak EIA/ISO manual says that `G49` moves the axis to remove the length offset. Z could move down by the tool length, near the part. The `safeRetract` option text says \"Z retract command before tool changes and at program end\", but the post wrote it only at program end and on Go home.\n\nFanuc and Doosan had the same order. A FANUC-family control can move Z on a `G49` block with no axis word. The issue asks to fix the two posts or to record them as not affected. This PR fixes them.\n\n## Tests\n\nPinning tests (new):\n- `setup_change::tool_change_retract::mazak_fanuc_doosan_retract_z_before_a_second_tool_g28`\n- `setup_change::tool_change_retract::mazak_fanuc_doosan_retract_z_before_a_second_tool_g53`\n- `setup_change::tool_change_retract::mazak_fanuc_doosan_retract_z_before_the_same_tool_called_again`\n- `setup_change::tool_change_retract::a_trip_home_is_not_followed_by_a_second_retract`\n- `setup_change::tool_change_retract::a_setup_change_stop_is_not_followed_by_a_second_retract`\n- `upright_after_tilt::tool_change_retract::fanuc_and_doosan_cancel_tcpm_before_the_tool_change_retract`\n\nRed before the fix: yes. On unchanged code, the three `retract_z_before` pins fail with `left: 0, right: 1` (no Z retract before the second G49).\n\nMutation results (each reverted, run, restored):\n- `mazak.cps` from upstream: the three `retract_z_before` pins are red.\n- `fanuc.cps` from upstream: the three pins are red.\n- `doosan-dnm.cps` from upstream: the three pins are red.\n- The `!zUp` guard removed (Doosan): `a_trip_home_...` and `a_setup_change_stop_...` are red (two retracts).\n- The `tcpmLeft` G49 removed (Fanuc): `fanuc_and_doosan_cancel_tcpm_before_the_tool_change_retract` is red.\n\nGates on the final head `ce23fdaa8` (base `a5e993538`):\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base a5e993538`: 149 steps, 0 failed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `app suites: example_catalog`, `first_part_programs`, `program_entry`, `thread_boss`, `thread_mill`: pass.\n- `cargo xtask gate light`: 6 steps, 0 failed.\n- Targeted heavy step (P1 under the safety floor): `cargo xtask gate heavy --only \"app heavy: example_catalog\"`: 1 step, 0 failed.\n- Upstream main moved to `a721fd4dc` during the work. It changed `crates/app/tests/conformance.rs` and `crates/post/tests/comment_escape.rs`. `git merge-tree` merges clean. Upstream's `conformance` passes on this fix (7 passed). The `comment_escape` change only replaces a fixed post count.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nEach change is one `G91 G28 Z0` line before a later preamble of a multi-tool Fanuc program. The default post is Fanuc. No Mazak or Doosan golden has two tools.\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/program_entry/fanuc_pause_home.nc` (+1)\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/thread_mill_external_m8_multi_form.nc` (+1)\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/thread_mill_m8_multi_form.nc` (+1)\n- `examples/first-part.nc` (+2), regenerated with `camcraft-cli process`\n- `examples/catalog/2d/adaptive-pocket/adaptive-pocket.nc` (+1)\n- `examples/catalog/2d/edge-work/edge-work.nc` (+3)\n- `examples/catalog/2d/first-part/first-part.nc` (+2)\n- `examples/catalog/2d/hole-work/hole-work.nc` (+4)\n- `examples/catalog/2d/slots/slots.nc` (+1)\n- `examples/catalog/3d/rough-finish/rough-finish.nc` (+2)\n- `examples/catalog/probing/probe-face/probe-face.nc` (+1)\n- `examples/catalog/multiaxis/indexed/indexed.nc`: after each tilted section the order is now `G49`, `G91 G28 Z0`, then `G90 G54 G40 G49 G80`. Before, it was `G90 G54 G40 G49 G80`, `G91 G28 Z0`, `G90`. Z is up before the preamble, and TCPM is off before the `G28`.\n\nThe catalog was regenerated with `cargo xtask catalog`. That command also rewrote the `.camproj` files: a project `version` 83 to 84, and float digits in the last place. These changes are not from this fix and are not in this PR.\n\n`crates/app/tests/program_entry.rs`: `z_homes` counts trip homes. It no longer counts the new lift immediately before a preamble `G49` line. The tests keep their intent: one trailing home, and the mid home plus the close home.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No run on a Mazak, Fanuc or Doosan control.\n- After a tilted section, the post writes `G49` before the lift, as its Go home did before. On a control where `G49` alone moves Z, that `G49` still runs before the lift. It runs in the same place as before this PR, so it is not new. A reference return under TCPM can alarm, so the post does not lift first.\n- Haas, Tormach and LinuxCNC also write `G49` in each section preamble. They are out of the scope of this issue. A follow-up issue asks for the same check.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone. No open PR changes `assets/posts/mazak.cps`, `fanuc.cps` or `doosan-dnm.cps`.\n\nDecision record: `docs/decisions/4341-mazak-retract-before-toolchange.md`.\nWriter record: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/4341#issuecomment-7218043395\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: The Mazak, Fanuc and Doosan DNM posts lift Z by the safe retract method before each later tool change, so the G49 of the next preamble never runs at the clearance height of the previous operation.\n\nFixes #4341\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
